<title>GREECE: NATL MORTGAGE BANK SETS RATES ON BONDS AT 11.20PCT.</title>
<headline>NATL MORTGAGE BANK SETS RATES ON BONDS AT 11.20PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek state National Mortgage Bank bonds due March 31, 1997 will be renewed for one year at an interest rate of 11.20 percent provided that they have not completed five years, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>National Mortgage Bank bonds issued in March, 1997 will carry annual interest rates of 11.20 percent and be subject to a 15 percent tax, it added. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
